   "obj": "1.1",
   "diff": 2,
   "q": "A technician is preparing to replace a Surface Pro battery. Which preparation follows the service guide before opening the device?",
   "choices": [
    "Shut down, discharge the battery, then unplug power",
    "Shut down, unplug power, then open at full charge",
    "Discharge the battery, leave the charger attached",
    "Put the device to sleep, discharge, then unplug"
   ],
   "answer": 0,
   "why": "The Surface guide requires full shutdown, battery discharge, and disconnection from power before repair. It also calls for ESD precautions.",
   "whyNot": {
    "1": "A charged battery still conflicts with the repair prerequisite.",
    "2": "The guide says to disconnect all power after discharge.",
    "3": "Sleep does not fully power off the device."
   },
